  id: cpu
  displayName: Processor (CPU)
  category: 0
  icon: {fileID: 0}
  mlLabel: cpu
  mlAliases: []
  specChips:
  - AM5
  - 6 cores
  - DDR5
  - 65 W
  shortDescription: The brain of the computer. It runs program instructions and does
    the calculations.
  whatItDoes: 'The CPU (Central Processing Unit) repeats a simple cycle billions
    of times a second: fetch an instruction from memory, decode it, execute it, and
    store the result.'
  keyFacts:
  - Fits in an AM5 socket on the motherboard
  - 6 cores / 12 threads
  - Needs a cooler and thermal paste
  - Works with DDR5 memory only
  installationSteps:
  - Lift the socket's retention lever.
  - Line up the gold triangle with the triangle on the socket.
  - "Lower the CPU straight down \u2014 never push."
  - Close the lever to lock it in.
  safetyTip: Hold the CPU by its edges and never touch the contacts underneath.
  model3DPrefab: {fileID: 8792363186054267891, guid: 8d38034e067075c4090d38ae9b4a8745, type: 3}
